/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-LITERATURE-2026-09-10.md-35-Prior work had equal-share allocation, a rate floor, a power cap and a pooled objective, and with continuous rate the occupancy term is a cost. We show that a discrete mode ladder inverts its sign, and that the resulting policy is consolidation rather than the interference-driven spreading the beam-hopping literature uniformly assumes. Load balancing is not refuted: it is optimal for the blocking objective it was designed for.
