/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-OPEN-DECISION-PROVISIONING-FIX-2026-09-10.md-4-## What is on the table
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-OPEN-DECISION-PROVISIONING-FIX-2026-09-10.md-5-Power is provisioned so the **nominal** signal-to-noise ratio equals the rate-target threshold exactly; the mode is then chosen from that same ratio **after** multiplying by the tenth-percentile fade quantile. The de-rating is never compensated at provisioning. Two independent adjudications, from different starting points and with the second given no knowledge of the first, agree this is a reference-frame slip rather than declared physics.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-OPEN-DECISION-PROVISIONING-FIX-2026-09-10.md-6-
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-OPEN-DECISION-PROVISIONING-FIX-2026-09-10.md:7:Its effect on the sealed model: **207,607 of 275,616 transmission instances (75.32 %) are credited nothing**, including **all 91,584** single-user instances.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-OPEN-DECISION-PROVISIONING-FIX-2026-09-10.md-8-
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-OPEN-DECISION-PROVISIONING-FIX-2026-09-10.md-9-## The proposed correction
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-OPEN-DECISION-PROVISIONING-FIX-2026-09-10.md-10-One expression, at two sites and their dense twins: provision against the same quantile the selection is later judged at — the threshold divided by the quantile instead of the threshold.
--
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-OPEN-DECISION-PROVISIONING-FIX-2026-09-10.md-23-One consequence to keep visible: at occupancy one the corrected rule delivers 1.362 times the rate target, because the bottom rung's spectral efficiency exceeds what was required. Over-delivery is credited by the current numerator. Whether that is the right numerator is a separate open question, currently under adversarial review.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-OPEN-DECISION-PROVISIONING-FIX-2026-09-10.md-24-
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-OPEN-DECISION-PROVISIONING-FIX-2026-09-10.md-25-## The three options
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-OPEN-DECISION-PROVISIONING-FIX-2026-09-10.md:26:**A — correct it, as a versioned successor.** The model then serves users the way its own design intent describes, and the geometry dependence the owner requires survives the change on the analysis so far. Cost: every efficiency figure, served count, prevalence census and coordination headroom the project holds must be recomputed. Nothing already sealed may be edited; a new lineage is generated.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-OPEN-DECISION-PROVISIONING-FIX-2026-09-10.md-27-
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-OPEN-DECISION-PROVISIONING-FIX-2026-09-10.md-28-**B — declare the current rule as the design.** Defensible only if the project is prepared to state in writing that its model deliberately provisions with zero fade margin and consequently credits nothing on three quarters of its transmissions, that a beam must be over-subscribed to be served, and that the reported service figures mean positive decoding time rather than rate-target attainment. I do not recommend this; the non-monotone service curve is the part a reviewer will not accept.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-OPEN-DECISION-PROVISIONING-FIX-2026-09-10.md-29-
