/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-ADJUDICATION-SYMBOL-GAPS-2026-09-09.md-1-# Controller adjudication — the four symbol gaps that block chapters 4 and 5
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-ADJUDICATION-SYMBOL-GAPS-2026-09-09.md:2:Recorded 2026-09-09. The unified symbol table registered four sealed concepts that have no glyph. All four are decided here. The binding constraint reported by the collision audit is that every unused Greek capital forms a case-pair with a live lowercase, so no free Greek capital exists, and multi-letter subscripts are forbidden by the table's own rules.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-ADJUDICATION-SYMBOL-GAPS-2026-09-09.md-3-
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-ADJUDICATION-SYMBOL-GAPS-2026-09-09.md-4-**The governing principle for all four: do not introduce a new letter. Use the superscript-marker mechanism the table already uses**, so each new symbol inherits an existing letter's meaning and adds a qualifier. This keeps the alphabet closed and makes every new glyph readable from its base letter.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-ADJUDICATION-SYMBOL-GAPS-2026-09-09.md-5-
--
