/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDINGS-AFTERNOON-2026-09-09.md-24-
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDINGS-AFTERNOON-2026-09-09.md-25-**The real defect is the beamwidth.** `TX_FULL_HPBW_DEG = 3.32°` is commented as retaining a HOBS full half-power beamwidth convention. The source's own equation uses `sin(theta_3dB)` with `theta_3dB = 0.058 rad` as an **off-axis angle**, not half of one. The engine registers a full span and halves it. The geometry is reproducible but **the HOBS attribution is unsupported**, and unlike the other cases the code still asserts it. Sensitivity is large: at 2° off-axis, halving or doubling the declared width moves the mechanism figure's endpoint from 9.17 Mbit/J to **zero** or to **13.08 Mbit/J**.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDINGS-AFTERNOON-2026-09-09.md-26-
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDINGS-AFTERNOON-2026-09-09.md:27:**The circuit constants are honestly declared, and that matters.** The audit confirms `338 mW` decomposes in its source as DAC 300 + mixer 19 + low-pass filter 14 + baseband amplifier 5 mW with the amplifier supply separate, and `200 mW` is a digital baseband precoder. But sealed amendment v1.8 **already** calls `0.35` a saturation efficiency, the satellite term a processing increment, and `50 Mbit/s` a power-control setpoint, and limits the energy boundary to named partial-payload components. So these are declared modelling assumptions, not physical claims dressed up as measurements. That is methodologically defensible provided the paper says so.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDINGS-AFTERNOON-2026-09-09.md-28-
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDINGS-AFTERNOON-2026-09-09.md-29-The two interruption constants are `UNVERIFIABLE_HERE`: their 3GPP annex could not be retrieved, and the audit correctly distinguishes inaccessible evidence from absent evidence. Under the primary interruption-off setting their effect is zero.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDINGS-AFTERNOON-2026-09-09.md-30-
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDINGS-AFTERNOON-2026-09-09.md-31-The ~20 s operational reserve is `UNSOURCED` as an empirical timing attribution only; the reserve itself is declared and has no direct physical-layer effect.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDINGS-AFTERNOON-2026-09-09.md-32-
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDINGS-AFTERNOON-2026-09-09.md-33-## 3. The unilateral comparator is degenerate, and both adjudications agree
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDINGS-AFTERNOON-2026-09-09.md:34:Two independent reviews, one per model family, reached the same verified number: the comparator selected a BASE configuration at **90 of 90 anchors**, not the 79 of 90 I reported. The eleven that certified successfully certified BASE with zero accepted updates; of the 79 that fell back, 37 had made tentative updates and discarded them.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDINGS-AFTERNOON-2026-09-09.md-35-
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDINGS-AFTERNOON-2026-09-09.md-36-So `FULL > S_UNI` is arithmetically the same test as `FULL > BASELINE`, which the figure already plots as its own curve. **The C4 conjunct cannot fail for any reason connected to coordination.**
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDINGS-AFTERNOON-2026-09-09.md-37-
--
