/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-PREDECLARATION-C3-SCREEN-2026-09-10.md-19-## Fixed before the run
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-PREDECLARATION-C3-SCREEN-2026-09-10.md:20:- **Both provisioning rules.** A result under the sealed rule alone would be measured on a model crediting nothing on three quarters of its transmissions; under the corrected rule alone it would prejudge a decision the owner has not taken.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-PREDECLARATION-C3-SCREEN-2026-09-10.md:21:- **Sealed learning rates and architectures, untouched**: first route 1.0e-2 with one hidden layer of eight and ReLU; second 1.0e-3 with 100-50-50 and tanh; third 1.0e-3 with 64-64 and ReLU; Adam at the sealed betas and epsilon; one deterministic full-batch update per route per source epoch. **If a route fails to train, that is the finding.**
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-PREDECLARATION-C3-SCREEN-2026-09-10.md-22-- **Two learner seeds**, reported seedwise, supporting no distributional claim.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-PREDECLARATION-C3-SCREEN-2026-09-10.md:23:- **Nine thousand source epochs. Checkpoints every 100. Full panel evaluation at exactly 500, 1000, 2000, 4000 and 9000. The contrast is reported at 9000**; the four earlier evaluations are trajectory and none may be reported as the outcome.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-PREDECLARATION-C3-SCREEN-2026-09-10.md-24-
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-PREDECLARATION-C3-SCREEN-2026-09-10.md:25:The separation matters: training an epoch and saving a checkpoint are nearly free, while evaluating the panel across arms, anchors and forty-eight boundaries is the expensive operation. **The budget therefore controls evaluation count, not epoch count** — which is why the horizon is nine thousand rather than the two thousand I first proposed. The owner made that point and it was correct.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-PREDECLARATION-C3-SCREEN-2026-09-10.md-26-
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-PREDECLARATION-C3-SCREEN-2026-09-10.md-27-- **A cost-driven early stop is legitimate** at whichever declared evaluation point was reached, with the measured figures that forced it. A stop chosen because a point looked favourable is not, and the distinction must be visible.
