/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-PREDECLARATION-C3-SCREEN-2026-09-10.md-31-- oscillating without settling → **that route's rate is too high**;
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-PREDECLARATION-C3-SCREEN-2026-09-10.md-32-- flat early and high → rate too low, or capacity or features are the limit, needing diagnosis rather than a rate change.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-PREDECLARATION-C3-SCREEN-2026-09-10.md-33-
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-PREDECLARATION-C3-SCREEN-2026-09-10.md:34:This exists so that the learning rates are not adjusted on the basis of the contrast they produce.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-PREDECLARATION-C3-SCREEN-2026-09-10.md-35-
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-PREDECLARATION-C3-SCREEN-2026-09-10.md-36-## Why a declared reporting point at all
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-PREDECLARATION-C3-SCREEN-2026-09-10.md:37:A previous pilot moved from −2.4 % at 200 epochs, through −1.6 % at 1000, to +15.6 % at 2000. Choosing among those after the fact would bias everything downstream. Looking early is fine and is the point of the trajectory; **choosing afterwards is not**.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-PREDECLARATION-C3-SCREEN-2026-09-10.md-38-
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-PREDECLARATION-C3-SCREEN-2026-09-10.md-39-## The primary deliverable is not the contrast
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-PREDECLARATION-C3-SCREEN-2026-09-10.md-40-It is the **training curves per route per arm**. Whether the routes converge, oscillate or are still climbing determines whether anything about the budget or the rates needs attention before a confirmatory run. A contrast from a route that never converged is not informative about that route.
