/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-ARCHIVE-AND-GROWTH-2026-09-09.md-29-## Which archive to use, and why it is not a freshness question
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-ARCHIVE-AND-GROWTH-2026-09-09.md:30:**Continue using the frozen archive.** Its purpose is reproducibility: a live archive grows daily, so the same experiment re-run tomorrow would build different worlds. The sealed declarations also carry a TLE date convention and forbid a TEST split, and selecting dates from a moving archive risks drawing a date that was meant to be held out.
