/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-SPAN-AND-C3-2026-09-10.md:16:The two sign counts answer different questions and must not be merged: on the selection-time objective the joint selector strictly improves on its seed at **20 of 20** anchors under both rules; on the forty-eight-boundary committed efficiency it is positive at 19 of 20 under the sealed rule and 14 of 20 under the corrected one.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-SPAN-AND-C3-2026-09-10.md-17-
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-SPAN-AND-C3-2026-09-10.md-18-One detail worth keeping: under the corrected rule the better unilateral endpoint delivers **fewer** bits than the archived one, 3.169 against 3.202 Tbit, while spending far less energy, 72,516 against 74,453 J. First-improvement trades bits for energy there.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-SPAN-AND-C3-2026-09-10.md-19-
--
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-4C-GATE-2026-09-08.md-6-2. **Selection-time grid:** stage-1 immediate scores are computed at the decision instant only (k = 0; the deployable controller's own view), stage-2 continuation for the top-M = 64 at the 5-boundary grid, the committed profile and all labels/endpoint at 48 boundaries (unchanged). KAT: the endpoint of a committed profile is bit-identical before/after; report the top-1 agreement between k = 0 scoring and the 5-boundary scoring on the rehearsal anchors.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-4C-GATE-2026-09-08.md-7-3. **Row-count check:** the stage-1 timing must report the catalogue row count; with the top-8 shortlist it must be ≈ 1 200 (≤ 1 500); if the count is ≈ 3 000 the shortlist was not applied — fix before timing.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-4C-GATE-2026-09-08.md-8-4. **Budget arithmetic (to verify at the gate):** ≈ 1 200 rows × 0.0014 s ≈ 1.7 s stage 1; 64 × 3 offsets × 5 boundaries batched ≈ 2 s; catalogue 3 s; selection + validation < 1 s → ≈ 7 s selection, well under 10 s; per anchor total (with 48-boundary commit of ≤ 14 arms) ≤ 60 s.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-4C-GATE-2026-09-08.md:9:5. **Reference state note (physics finding, not a change):** with the nearest-eligible carrier as a⁰ under rate-target physics, nearly every arm reassigns most users; the meaningful headroom comparisons are against U_all / S_UNI (unilateral local optimum) and S0, which the arm set contains. The carriers stay as sealed.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-4C-GATE-2026-09-08.md-10-6. **Gate:** if the real anchor still misses the 10 s selection budget after items 1–3, stop and report the dominating phase; no further approximation without a controller decision.
--
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-OPEN-DECISION-ARM-SET-2026-09-10.md-1-# Open owner decision — how to test "each component individually raises efficiency", with two reviewers disagreeing
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-OPEN-DECISION-ARM-SET-2026-09-10.md:2:Recorded 2026-09-10. Commissioned as a design consultation to `gpt-6-astra` at ultra effort and to `claude-fable-5-1`, both given the same neutral prompt that did not state my position. `DIAGNOSTIC_NOT_CLAIM`. Nothing was run; nothing sealed was modified. Related: [additive split], [pair insufficiency], [novelty closed].
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-OPEN-DECISION-ARM-SET-2026-09-10.md-3-
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-OPEN-DECISION-ARM-SET-2026-09-10.md-4-## The owner's requirement, as stated
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-OPEN-DECISION-ARM-SET-2026-09-10.md-5-Each of the three components must individually improve pooled efficiency over a control. Adding two or three interacts, so magnitudes will not add, but every subset must stay positive and the ordering must hold: FULL above any two, any two above the control.
--
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-OPEN-DECISION-ARM-SET-2026-09-10.md-8-- The phrase names **more than one experiment**, and interactions mean one does not establish another. Leave-one-out measures the *conditional* contribution of a component when the other two are present; single-component-only measures *standalone* benefit against a common control. These are different claims.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-OPEN-DECISION-ARM-SET-2026-09-10.md-9-- The intervention is **neutral-source substitution**, not deletion. "C1 only" means only that route's training source is informative while the other two are trained on neutral sources, with all heads retained and deployed. It never means removing a predictor. Any wording that implies presence-versus-absence is wrong.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-OPEN-DECISION-ARM-SET-2026-09-10.md-10-- **The reference matters and must be named.** Three candidates differ by orders of magnitude: the all-neutral control, the certified unilateral fixed point, and the geometry-only baseline. Neither of the outer two may silently stand in for the fixed point.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-OPEN-DECISION-ARM-SET-2026-09-10.md:11:- The sealed panel already covers five of the eight factorial cells — the full arm, the three pair arms, and the control. The three singles are missing.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-OPEN-DECISION-ARM-SET-2026-09-10.md-12-- **Neither would let a comfortable ordering license the conclusions the project wants.** Both refuse: that contributions are additive or independent; that the three-part architecture is necessary or better than a fairly trained simpler ranker; that the learned layer deserves credit for the prefix's several hundred per cent; that a large ablation gap is a large physical headroom.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-OPEN-DECISION-ARM-SET-2026-09-10.md-13-
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-OPEN-DECISION-ARM-SET-2026-09-10.md-14-## The disagreement
--
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.5-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md:1:# V025 priority declaration — v1.5 amendment (controller, sealed before any formal successor outcome; 2026-09-08 ≈ 18:25 UTC)
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.5-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md-2-
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.5-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md-3-v1.0–v1.4 are preserved unchanged. This amendment applies the fresh-context first-principles review (`FIRST-PRINCIPLES-REVIEW-CODEX-GPT6-ASTRA-2026-09-08.md`: `MINIMAL_DESIGN_MATCHES_PLAN=PARTIAL | SMALLEST_MATRIX=1 setting | HIGHEST_RESIDUAL_RISK=learner/information 0.90`) and pipeline audit A. No priority, constant, arm or margin changes; the order of execution and the uncertainty estimator do.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.5-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md-4-
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.5-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md:5:1. **Execution order and scope of the admission decision.** The training-admission decision (PHYSICS-GO) is made on the primary setting `a-r0` alone, as sealed in v1.1. The other 30 settings are **exploratory sensitivities**: they execute after `a-r0` completes, in the sealed priority order, within the remaining budget, and none of them can change the admission decision or the claim. The owner's requirement that the off-axis angle influence power and EE is demonstrated by the physics itself (a sealed KAT and figure of required power and EE versus off-axis angle under `a-r0`), not by matrix cells.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.5-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md-6-2. **Executable set-score decomposition (from the review's pass 1(d)).** For a configuration with changed-user set A relative to the anchor reference a⁰ and F = B − η_ref·E: unilateral increments dᵢ = F(aᵢ, a⁰₋ᵢ) − F(a⁰); interaction residual Ψ_A = F(a_A, a⁰₋A) − F(a⁰) − Σᵢ∈A dᵢ. C1(config) = Σᵢ∈A dᵢ (+ Φ), C3(config) = Ψ_A (credited to users by the Shapley allocation of the interaction game; pairs = Ψ/2 each), C2(config) = the declared continuation value excluding the immediate term. Identity: C1 + C3 = F(a_A) − F(a⁰) exactly (KAT). Factor arms: FULL = C1 + C2 + C3; DROP_C1 = C2 + C3; DROP_C2 = C1 + C3; DROP_C3 = C1 + C2 (additive), all in the same selector class and catalogue (stage-4 item 18).
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.5-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md-7-3. **Primary uncertainty estimator.** Because dates and learner seeds are crossed (audit A), the primary interval for every contrast is a **two-way pigeonhole bootstrap** over TLE dates × learner seeds with arms paired within each resample and ΣB/ΣE recomputed per draw; the one-way cluster bootstrap of v1.2 §3 and the delta-method interval become supplementary. For the learner-free physics matrix the primary is the one-way bootstrap over TLE dates.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.5-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md-8-4. **Claim-panel dates.** The successor's confirmation panel uses TRAIN dates that were never used by any successor development activity (probe, calibration, rehearsal, KAT, synthetic-real); the allocation manifest asserts this role-wise disjointness; overlap with legacy (old-physics) development dates is recorded, not forbidden, and the claim wording says so.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.5-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md:9:5. **TLE selection convention.** The legacy nearest-epoch rule (per NORAD, files date−1/date/date+1, |age| ≤ 24 h at episode start, future epochs allowed) is retained as an accuracy-first benchmark convention shared by all arms (`VERIFY_SOURCE`); it is documented as non-causal.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.5-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md-10-6. **Information contract for C3 (residual risk 0.90).** Before any successor training, the stages 6–8 contract v1 must state exactly what the learned heads observe and what the coordinator computes (candidate identities, load, shared capacity and interference, activation state, other users' proposed actions or a joint search), with the deployment-capability manifest; retrained ablations are the scientific claim, checkpoint knockouts are reported separately.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.5-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md-11-
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.5-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md-12-Seal: sha256 in the companion `.sha256` file.
